+/-!
+
+# The weight rule and the double sum as a finite sum
+
+At weight `μ = 0` the weight rule collapses the triple sum over Clebsch–Gordan coefficients to a
+single sum over `α`, and the zero-extended double sum `collapseSum` is a finite sum of the same
+summands.
+
+## i. Overview
+
+The projection identity of `SixJProjection` at `μ = 0`, `γ = K - k₁` has the triple sum
+`Σ_{α β ν} ⟨j₁ α j₂ β | j₁₂ 0⟩ ⟨j₁ α j₂₃ ν | J J⟩ ⟨j₂ β j₃ (K - k₁) | j₂₃ ν⟩` on the left. The
+weight rule (`cgCoefficient_eq_zero_of_ne`) forces `β = k₁ - α` in the first coefficient and
+`ν = K - k₃ - α` in the second, so that only the sum over `α ≤ k₁` remains (`sum_three_cg_eq`).
+Its summands are `collapseConst * collapseTerm` by `cg_three_eq` (`SixJTopWeight`), where
+`collapseTerm` still contains the Racah sum `racahSum b c k₃ (k₁ - α) (K - k₁)` of the third
+coefficient. On the other side, the zero-extended double sum `collapseSum` of
+`RacahDoubleSum` equals the finite sum of the `collapseTerm` over `α ≤ k₁`
+(`collapseSum_eq_sum_collapseTerm`), because the inner sum over `z` is `racahSum` after the
+conditions of its summands are matched to the nonnegativity of the factorial arguments
+(`Tterm_eq`).
+
+## ii. Key results
+
+- `sum_three_cg_eq`: the triple sum collapses to a sum over `α ≤ k₁`.
+- `Tterm_eq`: the summand `Tterm` in the form of the summand of `racahSum`.
+- `collapseSum_eq_sum_collapseTerm`: `collapseSum` as a finite sum of `collapseTerm`.
+
+## iii. Table of contents
+
+- A. The weight rule
+- B. The double sum as a finite sum
+
+## iv. References
+
+- G. Racah, *Theory of complex spectra. II*, Phys. Rev. 62, 438 (1942).
+
+-/
